@attribute [CustomPage("Components/Charts/Overview")]

<h1>Charts</h1>

<h2><code>ChartLegend</code></h2>
<p>A row of entries that names what a chart's colours and shapes mean; it wraps to more rows when it is too narrow. Each <code>LegendItem</code> has a swatch, a label and an optional <code>Marker</code> glyph such as ▲, so colour is not the only cue. With no items nothing is rendered.</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Swatch</th><th>Looks like</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Accent</td><td>A filled dot in <code>--color-accent</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Chip</td><td>A filled dot in <code>--color-chip</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Error</td><td>A filled dot in <code>--color-error</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Outline</td><td>A dashed ring in <code>--color-border-strong</code>, for something absent.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Line</td><td>A short dashed line in <code>--color-text-muted</code>, for a reference line.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<ul>
    <li>The list is labelled "Legend"; the swatches are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and as a prefix: <code>{TestId}-0</code>, <code>{TestId}-1</code>, … by position.</li>
</ul>

<p>Stories: <a href="./?path=/docs/components-charts-chartlegend--docs">ChartLegend</a></p>
